From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:06:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] tests: forcing schedules that need nothing of the engine
 but its public surface

hunt_bisect0 gets HUNT_MIDWALK: the snapshot handle's first scan is
stopped in the callback of its first entry while the writer commits on a
thread of its own, so the walk goes on into blocks whose published forms
the commit has replaced. hunt_cuts gets the second route of the
stale-cut hazard, a merge that lands with nothing frozen, forced by
holding a seal between its two phases, and a third that holds nothing and
makes the merge slow by the size of the partition. at_commit.sh builds in
directories of its own per invocation and has a port that takes the
landing out of keep_snap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011ZkLidS5BYuaBXVcvPAkdd
